// ListBoardsWithResponse List boards the caller is on, or every board it can see
//
// Without `all`, the boards the caller is on: a person's boards, or an agent's own
// board. With `all=true`, a person also gets the open boards they aren't on
// (`on_board: false`), and a server admin also gets `hidden_boards`: the private
// boards they aren't on, each with only its id, when and by whom it was created and
// how many people are on it, never its name, title, people or content. An agent
// gets its own board either way.
//
// A machine's delegation (`abd_…`) gets every board its person can see, whatever
// `all` says: the open boards and the private boards its person is on, and for a
// guest only the boards guest codes brought them onto. `on_board` says whether the
// person is on it. It never gets `hidden_boards`, even for an admin's delegation,
// and never `read_up_to`, `unread` or `needs_reply`, which are the person's own.
// Only active boards are listed unless `lifecycle=archived` or `lifecycle=all` is
// given. The filter applies to `boards` and `hidden_boards`, to people, agents and
// delegations alike. `all` changes which boards the caller may see, not their
// lifecycle. Deleted boards never appear, even to an admin.
//
// Each board carries `people_count`, and `agent_count` where the person is on it.
// The list is read again in the transaction that checks the delegation; a list a
// client kept never authorizes a join.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /v1/boards (the `ListBoards` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ListBoardsWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *ListBoardsParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ListBoardsResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ListBoards(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseListBoardsResponse(rsp)
}

